pve-smart-alert (0.5.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Release 0.5.0, milestone M5: one command installs the tool on a Proxmox
    VE node, a systemd timer runs the check every 30 minutes and after a
    reboot, a failed run is reported by a short mail at most once a day and
    once more after a reboot, and a purge removes every file of the tool.
    The acceptance passed on pve1 on 2026-10-18 and 2026-10-30 and on the
    cluster node pve5 on 2026-10-31 (ROADMAP.md). The user-visible changes of
    the test builds 0.5.0~dev1 to 0.5.0~dev5 are in CHANGELOG.md.

 -- Florian Punz <39314759+florianpunz@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 31 Oct 2026 20:45:00 +0100

pve-smart-alert (0.5.0~dev5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Pre-release of 0.5.0 for test hosts (ADR 0027), the content of the test
    build 0.5.0~dev4 (of milestone M6 the HPE Smart Array probe (ADR 0032),
    the notice about an unsupported controller with the number of monitored
    drives and the switch for the conditions of the tool (ADR 0031), the
    manual entries of the other pass-through types (ADR 0034) and the
    hardware support table; of milestone M7 the removal of control characters
    from drive strings, and the reference configuration installed at the path
    the tool names), with three fixes from the checks on pve1 of
    2026-10-18: a command interrupted with Ctrl+C says so on standard error
    and exits with status 130 instead of ending in a traceback;
    scripts/install.sh says what became of the package, whether the version
    is installed already, from which version to which it changed, that it was
    installed again, or that apt did not finish, and it refuses a package
    whose name is not pve-smart-alert or whose version is not the pinned one;
    a purge removes /usr/share/pve-smart-alert, so that a byte code cache
    written there by something other than the launcher no longer keeps the
    directory (ADR 0035); and, separately, the package installs the manual
    page, which until now the documentation named and no package carried.

 -- Florian Punz <39314759+florianpunz@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 30 Oct 2026 18:23:00 +0000

